<main class="pt-[140px] pb-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-[960px] px-6">
  <div class="text-center mb-12">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-accent/20 bg-accent/10 px-4 py-1.5 text-[13px] font-medium text-accent mb-6 uppercase tracking-wider">
      <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-accent animate-pulse"></span>
      Built for developers and AI agents
    </div>
    <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(32px,4vw,48px)] font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.1] mb-4">One API for 14M+ online businesses</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-white/60 max-w-[680px] mx-auto">ListSignal does two things. It keeps a record of every online business: what it is, what it runs, what it sells, what it earns. And it tracks what changes: a technology added or removed, hiring started, a revenue band moved, a website down. Both are one key away, by REST or from any MCP-capable AI agent. Free tier, no card, no sales call.</p>
  </div>

  <%!-- Quickstart --%>
  <section class="mb-12" id="quickstart">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Quickstart</h2>
    <ol class="space-y-2 text-white/70 text-[15px] mb-6 list-decimal list-inside">
      <li><a href="/signup" data-umami-event="signup_cta" data-umami-event-source="developers_page" class="text-accent hover:underline">Create a free account</a> and generate an API key in Settings. 1,000 lookups/month included.</li>
      <li>Call the API with your key:</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div>
        <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/35 font-semibold mb-2">The call</div>
        <pre class="rounded-xl bg-[#0C1429] border border-white/[0.07] p-5 text-[13px] text-emerald-200/90 overflow-x-auto h-full"><code>curl https://listsignal.com/api/v1/company/gymshark.com \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ls_YOUR_KEY"</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/35 font-semibold mb-2">What comes back (abridged)</div>
        <pre phx-no-curly-interpolation class="rounded-xl bg-[#0C1429] border border-white/[0.07] p-5 text-[13px] text-sky-200/90 overflow-x-auto"><code>{
  "data": {
    "domain": "gymshark.com",
    "http_title": "Gymshark Official Store",
    "estimated_business_model": "Ecommerce",
    "estimated_industry": "Fashion",
    "estimated_revenue": "$100M-$1B",
    "estimated_revenue_confidence": 0.91,
    "estimated_employees": "501-5000",
    "estimated_country": "GB",
    "http_tech": ["Shopify", "Klaviyo", "Gorgias", "Cloudflare"],
    "dns_email_provider": "Google Workspace",
    "shop_product_count": 1840,
    "shop_price_avg": 38.5,
    "hr_job_count": 42,
    "hr_departments": ["Engineering", "Marketing"],
    "http_emails": ["press@gymshark.com"],
    "http_last_seen_at": "2026-10-01 06:12:40",
    "changes": [
      {"field": "http_tech", "change": "added", "value": "Gorgias",
       "changed_at": "2026-09-28 11:02:17", "summary": "Gorgias added"},
      {"field": "hr_job_count", "change": "started", "value": "42",
       "changed_at": "2026-09-20 08:40:03", "summary": "started hiring (42 roles)"}
    ]
  }
}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre class="mt-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0C1429] border border-white/[0.07] p-5 text-[13px] text-emerald-200/90 overflow-x-auto"><code>curl "https://listsignal.com/api/v1/search?tech=Shopify&country=FR&hiring=true&limit=25" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ls_YOUR_KEY"

curl "https://listsignal.com/api/v1/changes?field=http_tech&change=added&value=Klaviyo&period=7d" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ls_YOUR_KEY"</code></pre>
  </section>

  <%!-- Endpoints --%>
  <section class="mb-12" id="endpoints">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Endpoints</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/[0.07] bg-white/[0.02] p-5">
        <code class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">GET /api/v1/company/:domain</code>
        <p class="text-sm text-white/60 mt-1.5">One company's full record: every field in the dictionary below under its own name, plus <code class="text-white/80">changes</code>, its last 20 recorded changes. Contact emails and phone on paid plans.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/[0.07] bg-white/[0.02] p-5">
        <code class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">GET /api/v1/search</code>
        <p class="text-sm text-white/60 mt-1.5">Filter companies by <code class="text-white/80">tech</code> (one name: a platform, a vendor, a WordPress plugin or a Shopify app), <code class="text-white/80">dns_tech</code>, <code class="text-white/80">email_provider</code>, <code class="text-white/80">country</code>, <code class="text-white/80">business_model</code>, <code class="text-white/80">industry</code>, <code class="text-white/80">revenue</code>, <code class="text-white/80">employees</code>, <code class="text-white/80">hiring</code>, <code class="text-white/80">shopify</code>. Ranked by traffic, up to 100 per page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/[0.07] bg-white/[0.02] p-5">
        <code class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">GET /api/v1/changes</code>
        <p class="text-sm text-white/60 mt-1.5">The change feed, newest first. Filter by <code class="text-white/80">field</code>, <code class="text-white/80">change</code> (added, removed, changed, started, stopped, down, back), <code class="text-white/80">value</code>, <code class="text-white/80">domain</code>, <code class="text-white/80">country</code>, <code class="text-white/80">business_model</code>, <code class="text-white/80">period</code> (24h, 7d, 30d, 90d). Every row carries a one-line <code class="text-white/80">summary</code>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/[0.07] bg-white/[0.02] p-5">
        <code class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">GET /api/v1/technologies</code>
        <p class="text-sm text-white/60 mt-1.5">Every tracked technology, plugin and app with live company counts, its category and its ecosystem.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/[0.07] bg-white/[0.02] p-5">
        <code class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">GET /api/v1/stats</code>
        <p class="text-sm text-white/60 mt-1.5">Live dataset statistics and the list of tracked fields, refreshed every 60 seconds. Citable.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-white/50 mt-4">Full machine-readable contract: <a href="/openapi.json" class="text-accent hover:underline">/openapi.json</a> (OpenAPI 3.1). Errors are RFC 9457 <code class="text-white/70">application/problem+json</code> with actionable detail, so agents self-correct in one retry.</p>
  </section>

  <%!-- Signals --%>
  <section class="mb-12" id="signals">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Signals: what changed</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] text-white/60 mb-4 leading-relaxed">Every business is re-checked on a weekly to monthly cadence. When a tracked field moves between two checks, one change row is recorded and never rewritten. You read them in the dashboard's Signals tab, export them as CSV, or page through <code class="text-white/80">/api/v1/changes</code>. A change is one of:</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/[0.07]">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead><tr class="bg-white/[0.02] text-left text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/35">
          <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Change</th>
          <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold">On</th>
          <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Reads as</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody class="text-white/70">
          <tr class="border-t border-white/[0.05]"><td class="px-5 py-3">added, removed</td><td class="px-5 py-3">http_tech, dns_tech, hr_departments, http_emails, http_social_links, ctl_subdomains</td><td class="px-5 py-3">Klaviyo added</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-white/[0.05]"><td class="px-5 py-3">changed</td><td class="px-5 py-3">estimated_business_model, estimated_industry, estimated_revenue, estimated_employees, estimated_country, verified_revenue, verified_employees, http_title, http_meta_description, dns_email_provider, shop_theme, shop_plus, shop_product_count (20% or more), news_last_funding_usd</td><td class="px-5 py-3">from $1M-$10M to $10M-$100M</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-white/[0.05]"><td class="px-5 py-3">started, stopped</td><td class="px-5 py-3">hr_job_count</td><td class="px-5 py-3">started hiring (12 roles)</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-white/[0.05]"><td class="px-5 py-3">down, back</td><td class="px-5 py-3">http_status</td><td class="px-5 py-3">website down (503)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- Data dictionary --%>
  <section class="mb-12" id="fields">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Every field, by name</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] text-white/60 mb-4 leading-relaxed">The same names everywhere: the API, the dashboard, the CSV. The prefix tells you where a value comes from. <code class="text-white/80">http_</code> the website, <code class="text-white/80">http_deep_</code> the deep pass over the site, <code class="text-white/80">dns_</code> DNS, <code class="text-white/80">ctl_</code> certificate logs, <code class="text-white/80">rdap_</code> the registry, <code class="text-white/80">bgp_</code> the hosting network, <code class="text-white/80">shop_</code> the store catalog, <code class="text-white/80">hr_</code> the job board, <code class="text-white/80">news_</code> news. <code class="text-white/80">estimated_</code> means a rule or a model produced it, and it comes with <code class="text-white/80">_confidence</code> and <code class="text-white/80">_evidence</code>. <code class="text-white/80">verified_</code> means a public registry said it. A <span class="text-emerald-400">signal</span> mark means a change on that field is recorded.</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/[0.07]">
      <table class="w-full text-[13px]">
        <thead><tr class="bg-white/[0.02] text-left text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/35">
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Field</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Type</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Meaning</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Signal</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody class="text-white/70">
          <%= for {name, type, _family, signal, doc} <- LS.Schema.Columns.doc_rows() do %>
            <tr class="border-t border-white/[0.05]">
              <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[12px] text-white/85 whitespace-nowrap"><%= name %></td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 text-white/40 whitespace-nowrap"><%= LSWeb.PageHTML.friendly_type(type) %></td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2"><%= doc %></td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 text-emerald-400"><%= LSWeb.PageHTML.signal_label(signal) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- MCP --%>
  <section class="mb-12" id="mcp">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">MCP server, for AI agents</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] text-white/60 mb-4 leading-relaxed">ListSignal speaks the Model Context Protocol natively. Point Claude, Cursor, or any MCP client at the endpoint and it gets three tools: <code class="text-white/80">listsignal_get_company</code> (the full record with its recent changes), <code class="text-white/80">listsignal_search_companies</code>, and <code class="text-white/80">listsignal_dataset_stats</code>.</p>
    <pre phx-no-curly-interpolation class="rounded-xl bg-[#0C1429] border border-white/[0.07] p-5 text-[13px] text-emerald-200/90 overflow-x-auto"><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "listsignal": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://listsignal.com/mcp",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ls_YOUR_KEY" }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
    <p class="text-sm text-white/50 mt-3">Streamable HTTP transport, stateless, JSON-RPC 2.0. The same key and quota as the REST API.</p>
  </section>

  <%!-- Limits & errors --%>
  <section class="mb-12" id="errors">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Plans and limits</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/[0.07]">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead><tr class="bg-white/[0.02] text-left text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-white/35">
          <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Plan</th>
          <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Calls / month</th>
          <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Rate</th>
          <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Contact emails and phone</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody class="text-white/70">
          <tr class="border-t border-white/[0.05]"><td class="px-5 py-3">Free</td><td class="px-5 py-3">1,000</td><td class="px-5 py-3">30 / min</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-white/40">Contactability only</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-white/[0.05]"><td class="px-5 py-3">Starter</td><td class="px-5 py-3">5,000</td><td class="px-5 py-3">60 / min</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-emerald-400">Included</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-white/[0.05]"><td class="px-5 py-3">Pro</td><td class="px-5 py-3">25,000</td><td class="px-5 py-3">120 / min</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-emerald-400">Included</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-white/50 mt-4">Only successful calls count against the quota. You never pay for a miss. Need more volume, webhooks, or bulk delivery? <a href="mailto:will@listsignal.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">Email us</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="text-center">
    <a href="/signup" data-umami-event="signup_cta" data-umami-event-source="developers_bottom" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-accent px-8 py-4 font-display text-[15px] font-semibold text-white shadow-[0_8px_28px_rgba(16,185,129,0.25)] hover:bg-accent-hover hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all">
      Get your free API key
      <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h10M10 5l5 5-5 5"/></svg>
    </a>
  </div>
</div></main>
